00:31:33,624 --> 00:31:37,778
one of the mistakes I made very early in my career and probably most of you make

566
00:31:37,778 --> 00:31:41,932
is you read something— whether it’s the inflation report from Canada, maybe a central bank report,

567
00:31:41,932 --> 00:31:44,864
You may have read the Financial Times or the Wall Street Journal

568
00:31:44,864 --> 00:31:48,777
and what you recognize is: Oh, this is really big data, this is a game changer.

575
00:31:52,880 --> 00:31:54,524
但实际上，你这样做时，你只是在强化自己从某些读物中形成的偏见。
When in fact, what you’re doing there

576
00:31:54,524 --> 00:31:57,196
is you’re simply enforcing a bias from something you might have read.

577
00:31:57,197 --> 00:31:59,458
你是在根据所读内容强化自己的理解。
You’re enforcing your understanding based on something you’ve read.

578
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:09,795
现在，在看执行方法前，我们先来回顾一两个其他原则，帮助理解：
Now, before we look at the execution methodology, let’s go over one or two other principles to understand:

580
00:32:11,940 --> 00:32:22,320
首先，当这些事件发生时，市场会出现流动性不足。流动性变得异常宝贵，
First and foremost, when we have these events, there are illiquid markets. Liquidity becomes a premium,

582
00:32:23,160 --> 00:32:27,340
参与者会退出市场。为什么要在未知风险面前承担风险呢？
participants disappear from the market. Why take on risk when there’s potential for the unknown?

584
00:32:28,380 --> 00:32:34,849
波动性上升的第二个原因是，随着价格上下波动——记得我们之前说的——会吸引越来越多的参与者。
The second reason volatility arises is that as price shifts, as price moves up and down—

585
00:32:34,849 --> 00:32:39,297
remember, as we said— it brings in more and more participants.

587
00:32:39,500 --> 00:32:43,990
所以，价格波动的动态会吸引更多参与者。
So, the dynamic of price shifting brings in more participants.

588
00:32:43,990 --> 00:32:47,133
话虽如此，我之前也提到过，
That said, as I’ve mentioned before,

589
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:56,580
波动性会引发更多波动性。
Volatility leads to more volatility.

590
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:03,240
第三个原因：不确定性——这才是真正的关键——
Another reason: uncertainty—this is the real key—

591
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:10,900
不确定性意味着人们会变得不那么在意价格。
uncertainty means people become less price-sensitive.

592
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:15,130
所以，当出现未知事件或市场担忧的事情时，人们不会考虑风险收益，他们不会考虑其他任何东西，只会想，‘我不在乎价格’
So, when there’s an unknown event or something the market is concerned about,

593
00:33:15,130 --> 00:33:20,544
people don’t think in terms of risk-reward, they don’t think in terms of anything other than,

594
00:33:20,544 --> 00:33:21,748
'I’m not price-sensitive;

595
00:33:21,748 --> 00:33:24,756
我必须立刻平仓，清空我的头寸。
I need to just get out and clear my book.’

596
00:33:24,760 --> 00:33:30,040
这一点很重要，因为这些是风险事件交易背后的核心规则和原则。
And that’s important to understand because, again, these are the underlying rules and principles that govern risk-event trading.

598
00:33:30,620 --> 00:33:34,020
市场会变得流动性不足。
The markets will be illiquid.

599
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:38,100
不同策略、不同玩家，对吧？
As prices shift, it’s going to bring in more and more participants. Different strategies, different players,

601
00:33:38,760 --> 00:33:40,280
耗尽性高点、耗尽性低点、趋势、趋势。
exhaustion high, exhaustion low, trend, trend.

602
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:43,760
这会带来更大的波动，因为波动本身会孳生波动。
It’ll bring more volatility because volatility breeds volatility.

603
00:33:44,460 --> 00:33:47,460
显然，不确定性意味着人们对价格不敏感。
And obviously, uncertainty means people are price-insensitive.

604
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:51,460
所以，你不想逆着某些风险事件操作。
So you don’t want to be fading certain risk events.

605
00:33:51,780 --> 00:34:01,926
现在，显然，我能给你的风险事件交易关键建议之一非常简单。
Now, obviously, note that one of the key tips I can give you for risk event trading is very simple.

607
00:34:01,926 --> 00:34:06,999
流动性不足意味着足迹图会变得更有参考价值。
A lack of liquidity implies the footprint becomes more relevant.

608
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:09,260
所以，流动性越低，足迹图作为工具就越有价值。
So less liquidity means the footprint is a far more valuable tool.

610
00:34:22,570 --> 00:34:29,210
流动性越低，你就能更清晰地看到某些交互。
Less liquidity means you’re going to see and spot certain interactions a lot clearer.

611
00:34:29,470 --> 00:34:32,550
色块线会更清晰，交互也会更清晰。
The color lines will be clearer. The interactions will be clearer.

612
00:34:33,390 --> 00:34:40,830
比如，数据公布后，市场上涨。
For example, the data comes out, the market moves up.

613
00:34:41,230 --> 00:34:44,230
你能立刻知道高点发生了什么。
You’re going to know straight away what’s happening at the highs.

615
00:34:44,990 --> 00:34:46,430
有人在抛售吗？有人在买入吗？
Is someone selling it? Is someone buying it?

616
00:34:46,430 --> 00:34:51,450
你只需要看简单的吸收、色块线或Delta色块。
You just need to see a simple bit of absorption, color lines, or color delta.

617
00:34:51,470 --> 00:34:53,924
因此，作为一个经验法则——
And that’s why, as a rule of thumb—

618
00:34:53,924 --> 00:34:55,833
也是我这次策略分享的建议——
and my tip for this strategy session—

619
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:04,190
所以要学会在经济数据、市场公告和央行事件中使用足迹图。
So learn to utilize the footprint during economic data, market releases, and central bank events.

